message: "If you use llm-spend-audit in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-spend-audit"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/llm-spend-audit"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/llm-spend-audit"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Three deterministic instruments for the standing rent an agent setup charges before it
  does any work: the preamble cost of starting a session, who burned the day's tokens
  split between live work and background services, and whether subscriptions already paid
  for are going undrawn. No LLM call, no network, no API key, no dependencies. It reads the
  transcripts the harness already wrote and does arithmetic on them. Documents the trap
  that makes naive calibration impossible: output_tokens is charged for the whole assistant
  message including thinking and tool calls, and the same usage object is repeated in every
  transcript record of that message, which inflated the project's own aggregates by 2.58x
  until it was found and locked behind a test.
keywords:
  - llm
  - token-accounting
  - cost-analysis
  - observability
  - claude-code
  - finops
